 "text": "Government | Blackford County, IN\nSkip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nCommunity\nDepartments\nGovernment\nPrograms & Activities\nServices\nHome\nGovernment\nGovernment\n9\n1\n1\n2\nAgendas & Minutes\nAccess easily searchable meeting agendas and minutes for various boards, commissions, and committees.\nAuditor\nThe County Auditor is in a real sense the chief accountant or controller of the county.\nClerk\nThe Blackford County Clerk is the recordkeeper of Circuit and Superior Court files.\nContact Us\nCounty Commissioners\nThe County Commissioners serve as the executive branch of county government.\nCounty Council\nThe seven member Blackford County Council oversees and administers the county budget. The council approves the annual budget, establishes the salaries for county officials and employees and authorizes spending to certain departments for specific purposes.\nJustice\nGather information on the sheriff's office, the courts, probation and more.\nRecorder\nThe Recorder's Office performs several duties of recording and preservation of documents such as deeds, mortgages, miscellaneous and DD 214 records for the citizens of Blackford County.\nTreasurer\nThe Treasurer’s office collects real estate, personal property, business personal property, mobile home and ditch assessment taxes.\nAgendas & Minutes\nAuditor\nClerk\nContact Us\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Council\nJustice\nCircuit Court\nCommunity Corrections\nProbation\nProsecutor\nSheriff's Office\nMerit Deputies\nCorrection Officers\nDispatch\nAdministrative St